Line 18; what coordinates should i use to center my rectangle at the center of the screen below the text at the top

The attached code had a drawRect() call and used CMU Graphics.

Response:

In CMU Graphics, drawRect takes the rectangle's left, top, width, and height. With the default 400-by-400 window, use:

drawRect(100, 120, 200, 150, fill='green')

That centers it horizontally and places it below the text at y=50. app.sqSize = 1000 does not change the window size.
